<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Minčeta Tower</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1319</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Minčeta Tower is the large round fortress at the highest, north-western corner of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dubrovnik">Dubrovnik</a>'s city walls. Begun as a four-sided tower in 1319, it was rebuilt in 1463–1464 after the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>, to plans by the Florentine architect Michelozzo, and completed by Juraj Dalmatinac. It is the city's most prominent landmark and the key to its landward defences.</p></div>
